@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Community health, made clearer"; }
<section class="hero-section">
    <div class="hero-copy"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse-dot"></span> Community health intelligence</div><h1>Building Healthier Communities Through Smarter Monitoring.</h1><p>Bring water quality, community health, and responsible early-warning signals into one shared view—so rural health teams can act with more context and confidence.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" asp-controller="Account" asp-action="Register">Explore platform <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a><a class="btn btn-quiet btn-lg" href="#how-it-works">Learn more <i data-lucide="play-circle"></i></a></div><div class="trust-row"><span><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i> Human-reviewed alerts</span><span><i data-lucide="lock-keyhole"></i> Privacy-aware by design</span></div></div>
    <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="AquaGuard monitoring illustration"><div class="visual-glow"></div><div class="visual-map"><span class="map-grid"></span><span class="map-route route-one"></span><span class="map-route route-two"></span><span class="map-point p-one"></span><span class="map-point p-two"></span><span class="map-point p-three"></span><div class="visual-card card-water"><i data-lucide="droplets"></i><div><small>Water source</small><strong>Safe today</strong></div></div><div class="visual-card card-alert"><span class="risk-dot risk-high"></span><div><small>Review signal</small><strong>Community follow-up</strong></div></div><div class="visual-card card-health"><i data-lucide="heart-pulse"></i><div><small>Health reports</small><strong>Trend monitored</strong></div></div></div></div>
</section>
<section class="stats-strip"><div><strong>8</strong><span>demo villages</span></div><div><strong>30+</strong><span>sample patient records</span></div><div><strong>20</strong><span>water-quality observations</span></div><div><strong>1</strong><span>shared health picture</span></div></section>
<section class="marketing-section" id="platform"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow text-teal">A calmer command centre</span><h2>Signals become context. Context supports action.</h2><p>AquaGuard helps teams keep the vital pieces together without overclaiming what the data can tell us.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="activity"></i></span><h3>Disease surveillance</h3><p>Spot changing patterns in reported, water-related illnesses across villages and time periods.</p><a href="#how-it-works">See monitoring <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="test-tube-2"></i></span><h3>Water quality</h3><p>Keep field measurements, missing tests, estimates, and confirmatory results clearly distinguished.</p><a href="#how-it-works">See water safety <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a></article><article class="feature-card"><span class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="siren"></i></span><h3>Early warnings</h3><p>Use transparent, rule-based signals to prioritize a human follow-up—not to diagnose an outbreak.</p><a href="#how-it-works">See early warnings <i data-lucide="arrow-right"></i></a></article></div></section>
<section class="workflow-section" id="how-it-works"><div class="workflow-content"><span class="eyebrow text-teal">How it works</span><h2>A practical loop for stronger community response.</h2><p>Designed for field teams and administrators who need a system that is clear on busy days and accountable on difficult ones.</p><div class="workflow-steps"><div><span>01</span><section><h3>Capture observations</h3><p>Record patient reports and water tests at the point of care.</p></section></div><div><span>02</span><section><h3>Review the full picture</h3><p>Compare health signals with water-quality history at village level.</p></section></div><div><span>03</span><section><h3>Follow up responsibly</h3><p>Use explainable warnings to guide testing, outreach, and investigation.</p></section></div></div></div><aside class="insight-panel"><div class="mini-chart"><span class="chart-bar b1"></span><span class="chart-bar b2"></span><span class="chart-bar b3"></span><span class="chart-bar b4"></span><span class="chart-bar b5"></span><span class="chart-bar b6"></span><span class="chart-line"></span></div><div class="insight-row"><span class="feature-icon"><i data-lucide="eye"></i></span><div><strong>Explainable by default</strong><p>Every alert carries its reason, evidence, and next recommended step.</p></div></div></aside></section>
<section class="marketing-section safety-section"><div class="safety-visual"><div class="water-ripple r1"></div><div class="water-ripple r2"></div><div class="safety-badge"><i data-lucide="shield-check"></i><strong>Safer water begins with better visibility.</strong></div></div><div class="safety-copy"><span class="eyebrow text-teal">Water safety + health</span><h2>Make the connections easier to see.</h2><p>AquaGuard brings source history, testing gaps, reported symptoms, and local risk into one reviewable workspace.</p><ul class="check-list"><li><i data-lucide="check"></i> Clear measured, missing, and estimated values</li><li><i data-lucide="check"></i> Village-level health and water context</li><li><i data-lucide="check"></i> Alerts that are not diagnoses or confirmed outbreaks</li></ul></div></section>
<section class="about-banner" id="about"><div><span class="eyebrow">About the initiative</span><h2>Technology in service of the people closest to the work.</h2></div><p>AquaGuard is a demonstration platform for thoughtful community-health monitoring in rural Northeast India. Its sample data is simulated and must never be treated as public-health surveillance.</p></section>
